; Origin: https://github.com/kcjengr/probe_basic
; License: GPL-3.0
; Local modification (lcnc-suite): the upstream version inferred rotary
; letters from the AXIS COUNT ([traj]axes: 4 -> A, 5 -> A C), which sends
; a nonexistent A-word on any 5-axis layout that isn't XYZAC (e.g. XYZBC
; nutating-head machines -> "Bad character 'A'"). Probe each rotary's INI
; section instead: [AXIS_x]MAX_LIMIT exists iff the axis is configured.
; Local modification (lcnc-suite, 2026-09-04): optional #1 = the A angle to
; return the table to (default 0 = the documented A=0 rule). In identity
; kinematics a fixture is a fixed point in the ROOM, the part's datum only
; at the table angle it was touched off at — the gateway passes that angle
; from the fixture's provenance stamp (command_policy.goto_zero_plan).
; Order: Z up, then the rotaries, THEN X/Y — the tip lands on the part's
; datum, not on the room point at A=0 ("G54 did not align anymore with the
; head — it stopped somewhere else").
o<go_to_zero> sub

M73
G90
G53 G0 Z0

o110 if [EXISTS[#<_ini[axis_a]max_limit>]]
    G0 A#1
o110 endif
o120 if [EXISTS[#<_ini[axis_b]max_limit>]]
    G0 B0
o120 endif
o130 if [EXISTS[#<_ini[axis_c]max_limit>]]
    G0 C0
o130 endif

G0 X0 Y0

o<go_to_zero> endsub

M2
